Negative control for the SELF-by-default acting-for segment (R6-3 · R6-3b · E15).

Puts the segment back to announcing an absence: the resting trigger says
"Acting for nobody", wears the layers icon, and is drawn exactly as loudly as a
segment that IS acting for someone. The operator's ruling is that acting for
nobody IS acting as SELF, and that self — 99% of every session — is the QUIET
default of the whole scope bar, loud only once a context is explicitly picked.

The mutant keeps every behaviour: the same rows from the same matrix, the same
greying, the same self row, the same search, the same scope pushes, the same
`acting-for` test hook. Only the resting state's words, icon and loudness go —
so a spec that asserts "the trigger renders" or reads its label back out of the
catalogue by key stays GREEN under it, which is the point: neither was ever
testing the self semantic. Only a case that reads the RESTING trigger's rendered
text for the self wording, and that separates the resting treatment from the
acting one, can tell the two apart.

Reds: acting-for-segment.spec.ts — the R6-3/R6-3b case(s) asserting that with no
context the segment names SELF and recedes, and that picking one makes it loud.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

  RE-ARMED by the developer seat, 2026-08-12, after the R6-12 fix moved the
  lines this patch's context quoted (the panel's marked row, its context-type
  tag and the dropped clear item). The MUTATION is unchanged — same three
  hunks, same defect, same claim — only rebased onto the current source. The
  earlier `acting_for_clear` hunk is gone with the item it changed: the way
  back out of a context is now the self row itself, so that key renders
